[thin] Functional hook nose and insertion ramp. The 2.6 mm total hook height comprises a 1.6 mm nose and 1 mm lead-in rise. Across the centered 5 mm blade entry, the 1 mm opening leaves a finite 0.6 mm nose above it. The sampled 0.72 mm places lie in that tool-purchase roof; the 1.91–2.04 mm places lie across the adjoining insertion profile. Physical release force and repeated use remain unqualified in rear-snap-retention/v3.
alternatives: Increasing roof thickness within this height reduces the requested blade opening or steepens the insertion ramp; increasing total hook height also deepens its receiving pocket into the fixed roof stock. Filling the entry removes centered tool access. The 2.6 mm flat retaining overlap remains on each side of the entry.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/rear-equipment-caps/asse-snap-cap.step
